            </profile>
            <profile id="6393-3af5-0837-23f1" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="b792-78e1-7b03-d4d6" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Armed with a hand weapon and shield or dagger axe. May have light armour (+2). May have thrusting spear instead of dagger axe. Light Infantry. Chariot Runners: up to one unit of 10 models per chariot fielded; initially deployed within 6" of the chariot model. In the Army of Sanxingdui the Retinue becomes an Elephant Retinue (the Chariot Runner rules apply to Elephants instead). (The Art of War p.13)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
