            <profile id="aa8a-4fae-9d06-f0e4" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="b792-78e1-7b03-d4d6" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">An unarmed driver and up to two crew armed with javelins or bows (+2 pts) per crewman. Crew may have light armour (+2 pts). Elephants. Designer's note: although elephants were present in Shang and Pre-Shang China there is no definite evidence they were used for warfare; offered for speculating "what if". 0-1 (the Army of Sanxingdui may have up to one per 1,000 points). (The Art of War p.14)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <infoLinks>
            <infoLink id="24e8-94d5-68c7-618d" name="Elephants (Art of War)" hidden="false" targetId="4a67-d018-0b7c-18d5" type="rule"/>
