  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="a3b1-397d-d4a9-b508" name="Early Chinese (Art of War) - List Notes" publicationId="b792-78e1-7b03-d4d6" hidden="false">
      <description>EARLY CHINESE (The Art of War, pp.12-14): Pre-Shang and Early Shang, Later Shang and the Army of Sanxingdui. Special rules: Auspicious Conditions (roll a D6 at the start of the game: 1 = automatically fail the first D3 Leadership tests; 6 = automatically pass them), Casting the Oracle Bones, Off with their heads!. Percentage limits are by points. "May only have one selected option per 1,000 points" for Special Units is documented only.

ARMY COMPOSITIONS (pick one in the Army composition list):
[Early Chinese - Pre-Shang and Early Shang]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Infantry: at least 50%
  Special Units: up to 25%
  PRE-SHANG AND EARLY SHANG DYNASTY (Xia and earlier, or Early Shang before chariots, c.1300 BCE). Characters up to 25% (at least one army commander, the character with the highest Leadership; characters may not have chariots). Infantry at least 50%. Special Units up to 25% (one selected option per 1,000 points). No chariotry.
[Early Chinese - Later Shang]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Chariotry: up to 50%
  Infantry: at least 25%
  Special Units: up to 25%
  LATER SHANG DYNASTY (after the introduction of chariots c.1300 BCE). Characters up to 25% (at least one army commander). Chariotry up to 50%. Infantry at least 25%. Special Units up to 25% (one selected option per 1,000 points).
[Early Chinese - Army of Sanxingdui]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Chariotry: up to 50%
  Infantry: at least 25%
  Special Units: up to 25%
  ARMY OF SANXINGDUI. Characters up to 25% (one army commander; no chariots, but may be mounted on Elephants instead, the points taken from the Chariots section). May take Frightening Masks (+20 pts: the character causes fear). Chariotry up to 50%: no chariots, but Elephants may be taken instead (Chariot Retinue becomes Elephant Retinue; Chariot Runners rules apply to Elephants). Infantry at least 25%. Special Units up to 25%, with up to 1 Elephant per 1,000 points. Fuhao is not available.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
